From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] uiautomationcore: pattern caching, AutomationElementMode_None (3582)

uiautomationcore: pattern caching in cache requests, AutomationElementMode_None

UiaGetUpdatedCache gets one column per cached pattern: empty if a node does not support the pattern, else the
values of the pattern's properties (a table of each pattern's UIA_<Pattern>*PropertyId family and its
IsPatternAvailable property). The COM client reads them back into the element's cached properties,
IUIAutomationElement::GetCachedPattern/GetCachedPatternAs return a pattern object whose Cached* getters read
them (UIA_E_NOTSUPPORTED if the pattern was not requested, no object if unsupported). AutomationElementMode_None
is accepted: such elements answer only from the cache (Current* calls give UIA_E_NOTSUPPORTED).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01XZFS4SPPzeH5d2c1MuzqCS
---
